//@version=6
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// LEGACY FOREX TRADER — COMPLETE VISUALISER
// v1 2026-09-05  ·  v2 2026-09-06 (tick #8 code audit — SYSTEM.md FINDING 17)
//                ·  v3 2026-09-06 (tick #9, the stop-width gate — FINDING 18)
//                ·  v4 2026-09-06 (tick #10, the touch tolerance — FINDING 19)
//
// NOT ONE NUMBER IN THIS FILE HAS EVER COME FROM A RUN. This workstream has no runId. Every
// default here is either a source quote or a labelled interpretation; nothing is a measurement.
//
// A faithful, mechanical rendering of MAMBA's system — the New York / NQ+YM trader.
// See legacy-forex/SYSTEM.md for every rule with its verbatim quote and timestamp.
//
// ⚠ THE COMMITTED TRANSCRIPT CORPUS IS TWO TRADERS, NOT ONE (SYSTEM.md FINDING 6, 2026-09-05).
//   Eight numbered modules + five NY live streams are MAMBA — NQ/YM, New York, 5m/15m. That is
//   this file. Four "videoNNNN" live streams + module 4 are COACH LUCA — gold (MGC), Asia session,
//   1m-1h, ATR stops, fair value gaps, a 200 MA. NOTHING from Luca belongs in this indicator.
//   (Module 4 is the one exception this file draws on, and only where Luca is quoting Mamba's own
//   numbers back — flagged at the point of use.)
//
// INDICATOR, not a strategy — it takes no positions. It draws every element of his method and a
// dashboard that names the exact condition currently blocking a trade.
//
// RUN IT ON: NQ or YM (or NAS100 / US30), 5-minute or 15-minute chart. Nothing else — he is
// emphatic that those two instruments and those two timeframes are the entire universe:
//   "NQ and YM is the only thing we trade. We trade nothing else."      (3._WHAT_TO_TRADE 01:45)
//   "15 and 5 is the only place we're ever going to be."                (5._ANALYZING_TIME_FRAMES 03:18)
//
// ── HIS STACK, IN ORDER ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//   1. SESSION    New York only, first entry 09:30 ET      (8. 00:14 / 00:44)
//   2. STRUCTURE  HH+HL = longs only. LL+LH = shorts only.
//                 Anything else is consolidation = NO TRADE (6. 01:53 / 06:22)
//   3. LEVEL      support = floor, resistance = ceiling, validated by repeated DISTINCT touches;
//                 a broken level flips role                 (7. 00:27 / 00:47 / 01:51)
//   4. BREAK      price breaks the level in the structure's direction. The retest is a BONUS,
//                 not a gate: "we don't need it to come back and retest"  (7. 05:35)
//   5. VOLUME     must be present. "If there's no volume, there's no trading."  (9. 07:51)
//   6. STOP       just beyond the broken level, never the far one — AND capped: a structural stop
//                 wider than his per-instrument maximum REJECTS the setup — "64 points, my
//                 account's gone if I do that"              (11. 00:07 / 01:26)
//   7. TARGET     NOT a fixed 1:3-1:5. It is the mean achieved R of his last ~6 closed trades,
//                 losses scored 0, rounded, recomputed daily — "we are averaging a one, two,
//                 three... which means we are going to go for one, two, threes"  (10. 00:38-05:43)
//                 1:3-1:5 (9. 05:53) is where that output usually LANDS, not the rule.
//   8. MANAGE     break-even at +1R (+1.5R at the latest) is the only part he states as
//                 non-negotiable; what happens ABOVE that is under-determined in the source —
//                 see the TRAIL note below. (11. 02:13 / 03:59 / 06:38 / 08:02 / 09:01)
//   9. LIMIT      max 2 trades/day, 3 exceptionally — and the cap counts ACROSS NQ+YM together,
//                 not per instrument (video1263885792 03:58). Realised rate is ~0.6-0.8 per
//                 session, about a third of the cap (10. 00:38 / 02:22).
//
// ── THE TRAIL IS UNDER-DETERMINED IN THE SOURCE — v2 STOPS PRETENDING OTHERWISE ────────────────
// Module 11 supports THREE different trail rules, in the same nine minutes, and v1 silently
// hard-coded one of them as if it were the rule:
//   (a) STEP EVERY +1R — "Every time this thing moves up in the same distance as our stop loss,
//       which is 25 points, we're going to adjust our stop loss" [02:13]; "as price starts to
//       push up even higher, you just adjust with it" [03:59].
//   (b) FREEZE AT +1R — what his own worked example actually does: at 1:5 he moves the stop to
//       1:1 and leaves it. "We're now at a one to five... we're going to put that down to a one
//       to one" [06:27-06:38].
//   (c) BREAK-EVEN ONLY — offered explicitly as a complete alternative: "or don't adjust your
//       stops at all" [09:01], with the floor being "at worst, at the least, please put your
//       stops to break even at a one to one point five at the worst" [08:02-08:19].
// Only the break-even floor is stated as non-negotiable. The mode is now an INPUT, defaulting to
// (b) because that is the one he demonstrates rather than describes, and the dashboard names the
// live mode. This is a source ambiguity, not a modelling choice — do not resolve it by taste.
//
// ── ONE CONTRADICTION, DRAWN RATHER THAN RESOLVED ─────────────────────────────────────────────
// The modules gate direction on structure (bullish -> buys only). The live streams show him
// pre-marking a break level on BOTH sides of BOTH instruments and taking whichever goes:
//   "Be prepared for all four positions on the screen."     (video1263885792 01:28)
// The course gate is left ON by default. "Show counter-structure bracket" draws the level he would
// have marked but this gate forbids, as a dotted line, so the disagreement is visible on the chart.
//
// ── DELIBERATELY NOT DRAWN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// No higher-timeframe bias filter. That is not an omission — he rules it out explicitly:
//   "There's no overall bias. We're not seeing what the daily is doing."   (5. 03:00)
// This is the opposite of the War Formation and 3M systems, and the three must not be mixed.
//
// ── WHAT v2 CHANGED, AND WHY (SYSTEM.md FINDING 17) ───────────────────────────────────────────
//  1. TOUCH COUNTING WAS COUNTING BARS, NOT TOUCHES, AND COUNTED THE LEVEL'S OWN PIVOT WINDOW.
//     v1 incremented once per BAR whose high or low sat within tolerance of the level, scanning
//     all 200 lookback bars including the pivot's own formation neighbourhood. The pivot bar
//     scores a touch by construction (|high - lvl| = 0), and each of the 2*pivLen neighbours
//     scores one whenever the local swing spans less than the tolerance. So "3 touches" could be
//     — and on a quiet swing usually was — satisfied the instant the pivot confirmed, with ZERO
//     revisits. His own definition is distinct visits: "one touch two touch three four five six
//     seven touches with those wicks" (7. 00:47). v2 counts distinct band ENTRIES and excludes
//     the pivot's own +/- pivLen window. BOTH counts are shown side by side so the size of the
//     correction is visible on a live chart instead of argued about.
//     ⚠ THIS MAY TAKE THE SIGNAL COUNT TO ZERO. That is HARD LESSON 8's tell and it is expected
//     to be checked, not assumed either way. `minTouch` is NOT retuned here — retuning it without
//     a measurement would be exactly the fabrication this project forbids.
//  2. THE ROLE FLIP WAS ADVERTISED IN THE HEADER AND ABSENT FROM THE CODE. "Support broke and
//     then became resistance... they turn into each other and they do very often" (7. 01:51-02:19),
//     "a break and a retest of support into resistance" (7. 07:14). v2 tracks and draws flipped
//     levels. It does NOT let them fire signals by default — that would change the signal set and
//     the audit at the same time.
//  3. INTRABAR SEQUENCING. v1 moved the stop using THIS bar's close and then tested THIS bar's
//     low against the moved stop, so a bar that closed at +2R could book a "+1R trail" exit on a
//     low that happened before the run-up. v2 manages on the PREVIOUS bar's R.
//  4. AN AMBIGUOUS BAR (target and stop both touched) BOOKED THE WIN. Now books the stop, the
//     conservative convention. It matters because achieved R feeds the rolling-mean target.
//  5. ONE MAX-STOP FOR TWO INSTRUMENTS. "Mamba uses 20 points on NASDAQ, let's say 30 points on
//     YM" (4. 04:09 — Luca quoting Mamba). 30 points is ~0.14% of NQ and ~0.07% of YM: the same
//     number is a materially different gate. v2 resolves per instrument and shows which is live.
//
// ── WHAT v3 CHANGED, AND WHY (tick #9 — SYSTEM.md FINDING 18) ─────────────────────────────────
// v2 fixed the max-stop CAP per instrument and left the PADDING in different units from the cap.
// The padding is a percentage of price; the cap is absolute index points. At the price levels he
// is actually trading — both of which are read off his own screen in the committed transcripts —
// the padding alone eats most of the entire risk budget before any structural distance counts:
//
//   NQ 24,954.50 (4. 03:06)   pad 0.05% = 12.48 pts = 62.4% of the 20-pt cap  -> 7.5 pts left
//   YM 46,942    (4. 07:23)   pad 0.05% = 23.47 pts = 78.2% of the 30-pt cap  -> 6.5 pts left
//
// So `useMaxStop` (ON by default) was rejecting any break whose close sat more than ~7 points
// beyond the level it had just broken. And because the pad SCALES WITH PRICE while the cap does
// not, the gate becomes mathematically unsatisfiable — pad alone >= cap, so no setup can pass at
// any distance — at NQ 40,000 and YM 60,000. The indicator had a built-in expiry date.
//
//  6. PADDING IS NOW IN HIS UNITS, NOT PERCENT. Nothing in the source states a padding distance:
//     "our stop loss is below where it would come back to retest" (7. 05:43), "just needs to
//     simply start just below that support" (11. 00:15). The pad is the word "just", and at NQ it
//     was consuming half of the 25-point stop that whole sentence describes. The one padding
//     quantity the source DOES define is the tick — 0.25 pts on NQ, 1 pt on YM (4. 02:06 / 07:07)
//     — so the default is now one tick (1.0% and 3.3% of the respective caps). This is the
//     minimal source-expressible reading of "just below", labelled as an interpretation, not a
//     stated rule. The % mode is retained so v1/v2 behaviour stays reproducible for diffing,
//     exactly as `touchMode` retains v1's counting.
//  7. THE NQ CAP DEFAULT FOLLOWED THE WEAKER SOURCE. 20 pts comes from module 4 [04:09], which is
//     LUCA DESCRIBING what Mamba uses. Module 11 is Mamba DEMONSTRATING: "That's a 25 point stop
//     loss, which is solid. That's actually a really good number" [00:20-00:23], "we have a 25
//     point stop" [01:43] — and a 20-pt stop at [06:50]. A 20-pt cap therefore REJECTS the exact
//     worked example module 11 teaches. This file already set a precedent for this exact kind of
//     ambiguity in v2's trail-mode fix — default to the one he DEMONSTRATES rather than describes
//     — so the NQ cap default moves 20 -> 25. The source brackets it at 20-25 and refuses 64
//     ("my account's gone", 11. 01:26); it does not pin it, and the input is where that lives.
//     YM's 30 is unchanged and remains SINGLE-SOURCED from Luca — module 11 has no YM example.
//  8. THE PAD FORMULA WAS WRITTEN TWICE. The projection used `padNow` and the trade-open block
//     recomputed the same expression inline, so any change to one silently diverged from the
//     other. One definition now.
//
// ── WHAT v4 CHANGED, AND WHY (tick #10 — SYSTEM.md FINDING 19) ────────────────────────────────
// v3 spent a whole tick getting the stop PADDING into the cap's units. It never asked what units
// the TOUCH TOLERANCE was in. Same defect class, one order of magnitude larger, and it had been
// sitting in the file since v1:
//
//   NQ 24,954.50 (4. 03:06)   tol 0.10% = 24.95 pts  → band 49.9 pts = 200% of the 25-pt cap
//   YM 46,942    (4. 07:23)   tol 0.10% = 46.94 pts  → band 93.9 pts = 313% of the 30-pt cap
//
// THE CONSEQUENCE, AND IT IS AN OUTRIGHT CONTRADICTION BETWEEN TWO GATES:
//   stop budget = cap − pad = 24.75 pts (NQ) / 29.0 pts (YM) — the most a break may sit beyond
//   the level and still be accepted by the stop-width gate. The touch tolerance is 24.95 / 46.94.
//   tol > budget on BOTH instruments. So EVERY break this system is capable of trading lies
//   inside the band its own level definition still calls "touching" — "price can't break it,
//   it's stuck" (7. 00:47). One gate calls the bar a touch; the other calls it a break; they are
//   describing the same bar and the same level. The tolerance is also 100× the pad on NQ and 47×
//   on YM: v3 tuned the level's padding to a quarter of a point while the level's own identity
//   was fuzzy to twenty-five.
//
//   9. TOLERANCE IS NOW A FRACTION OF THE LIVE MAX STOP, NOT A % OF PRICE. The source states no
//      width. It states that the level IS a zone — "support zones" (7. 01:21), "you make this
//      little thicker because it's the whole thing" (7. 04:35) — and never how thick. So the
//      number is an interpretation either way, and the only defensible constraint available is
//      COMMENSURABILITY: a level's own width must be smaller than the stop that has to sit
//      outside it, or "just below that support" (11. 00:15) is undefined. Anchoring tolerance to
//      the cap enforces that by construction and removes the price-scaling drift for free. The
//      default 0.20 (5 pts NQ, 6 pts YM) is an INTERPRETATION, exposed as an input and
//      pre-registered as a one-dimensional test — it is NOT a measured optimum.
//      Why not ATR, the obvious volatility-relative fix: ATR stops are COACH LUCA's, and nothing
//      from Luca belongs in this indicator (see the corpus warning at the top).
//      % mode is retained and reproduces v1-v3 EXACTLY, including its own minor defect — it sizes
//      the band off the CURRENT bar's `close` rather than off the level, so a fixed level's touch
//      count can change on a bar where nothing happened near it. Kept for diffing, not for use.
//  10. THE BREAK MAY NOW BE REQUIRED TO CLEAR THE BAND. OFF by default: turning it on changes the
//      signal set, and a correction tick does not audit and alter what fires at the same time
//      (v2's precedent with `flipTrades`). Under v1-v3 tolerance this option was not merely off,
//      it was UNSATISFIABLE — clearing a 24.95-pt band leaves −0.2 pts of stop budget on NQ. At
//      v4's tolerance it leaves 19.75, so it becomes a real pre-registered test for the first time.
//  11. INSTRUMENT RESOLUTION MOVED ABOVE THE LEVEL BLOCK, because the tolerance now depends on it.
//      No behaviour change: it reads only inputs and `syminfo`.
//
// ⚠ WHAT v4 DOES **NOT** CLAIM: the DIRECTION of the bias on the touch count. A too-wide band
//   makes each bar easier to score as a touch, and simultaneously makes distinct VISITS harder to
//   separate — price must leave a 50-pt band entirely before a new visit can begin. The two push
//   opposite ways and no arithmetic settles which dominates. That is a chart measurement, and the
//   dashboard row + data-window plots added here exist so it can be made instead of argued.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

indicator("Legacy Forex Trader — Complete Visualiser", overlay=true, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500, max_boxes_count=500)

// ── INPUTS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
gS = "Session"
useSession = input.bool(true,  "New York session only",            group=gS)
sessTime   = input.session("0930-1600", "Session (ET)",            group=gS)
sessTZ     = input.string("America/New_York", "Timezone",          group=gS)

gStruct = "Market structure"
pivLen   = input.int(5,  "Swing pivot strength (bars each side)",  group=gStruct, minval=1)

gLvl = "Support / resistance"
tolMode  = input.string("Fraction of the live max stop (v4 default)", "Touch tolerance unit", options=["Fraction of the live max stop (v4 default)","% of price (v1-v3 behaviour)"], group=gLvl,
     tooltip="v4: the source never states a zone width, only that a level IS a zone (7. 01:21 / 04:35). In % mode the band was ±24.95 pts on NQ and ±46.94 on YM — wider than the entire stop budget, so every tradeable break was still inside the band the counter calls a touch. Anchoring to the cap makes the two commensurable by construction. % mode reproduces v1-v3 exactly (including its close-anchoring defect) and is here for diffing, not for use.")
tolFrac  = input.float(0.20, "Touch tolerance, fraction of the live max stop", group=gLvl, minval=0.01, maxval=1.0,
     tooltip="0.20 → ±5 pts on NQ (cap 25), ±6 on YM (cap 30). This is an INTERPRETATION — the source gives no width — exposed as an input and pre-registered as a one-dimensional test. It is NOT a measured optimum and must not be quoted as one. The only thing arithmetic pins is the ceiling: tolerance must stay below the stop budget (cap − pad).")
touchTol = input.float(0.10, "Touch tolerance, % of price (v1-v3 behaviour only)", group=gLvl,
     tooltip="Legacy. 0.10% of price = 24.95 pts at NQ 24,954.50 and 46.94 at YM 46,942 — see SYSTEM.md FINDING 19.")
breakClears = input.bool(false, "Break must clear the tolerance band", group=gLvl,
     tooltip="OFF by default on purpose. v1-v4 score a break on a close one tick past the pivot, while the counter still calls that bar a touch of the same level — the two gates contradict each other. Turning this on resolves it in the source's favour ('price can't break it', 7. 00:47) but CHANGES THE SIGNAL SET, so it is a pre-registered test, not a fix applied here. Under v1-v3 tolerance it was unsatisfiable outright.")
minTouch = input.int(3,      "Touches to validate a level",        group=gLvl, minval=2,
     tooltip="v2: this now gates on DISTINCT visits, not bars-in-band. It is a much stricter test than v1's. NOT retuned — the correct value is a measurement nobody has made yet. v4 audit: 3 is the one level-gate number the source DOES support — 'we have all these touches one two three is resistance' (7. 04:31), against 7 (00:47), 4 (01:04) and 8 (01:41) elsewhere. It is a floor he shows, not a threshold he states.")
touchMode= input.string("Distinct visits (v2, his definition)", "Touch counting", options=["Distinct visits (v2, his definition)","Bars in band (v1 behaviour)"], group=gLvl,
     tooltip="Kept switchable so v1's behaviour is reproducible and the two can be compared on one chart. 'Bars in band' is known wrong; it is here for diffing, not for use.")
showFlip = input.bool(true,  "Draw flipped levels (broken support -> resistance)", group=gLvl)
flipTrades=input.bool(false, "Allow flipped levels to fire signals", group=gLvl,
     tooltip="OFF by default on purpose: turning it on changes the signal set, and v2's job was to correct the level test, not to alter what fires.")

gVol = "Volume"
useVol   = input.bool(true, "Require volume",                      group=gVol)
volLen   = input.int(20,    "Volume average length",               group=gVol)
volMult  = input.float(1.0, "Volume must exceed avg ×",            group=gVol)

gRisk = "Risk"
padMode   = input.string("Ticks beyond the level (v3 default)", "Stop padding unit", options=["Ticks beyond the level (v3 default)","% of price (v1/v2 behaviour)"], group=gRisk,
     tooltip="v3: the source never states a padding distance — it says the stop goes 'just below that support' (11. 00:15). The pad is the word 'just'. In % mode it was 12.5 pts on NQ and 23.5 pts on YM, i.e. most of the whole max-stop budget. The tick is the one padding quantity module 4 actually defines, so ticks is the default. % mode is kept for reproducing v1/v2, not for use.")
padTicks  = input.float(1.0,  "Padding, ticks beyond the level", group=gRisk, minval=0,
     tooltip="1 tick = 0.25 pts on NQ, 1 pt on YM (4. 02:06 / 07:07). This is an INTERPRETATION of 'just below', not a stated rule — vary it in a forward test.")
stopPad   = input.float(0.05, "Padding, % of price (v1/v2 behaviour only)", group=gRisk)
useMaxStop= input.bool(true,  "Reject setup if stop too wide (11. 01:26)", group=gRisk)
instMode  = input.string("Auto from ticker", "Instrument", options=["Auto from ticker","NQ / NAS100","YM / US30"], group=gRisk,
     tooltip="Auto matches the ticker string. Per SYSTEM.md FINDING 15 a ticker string is never trusted silently, so the resolved instrument is printed on the dashboard — check it by eye.")
maxStopNQ = input.float(25.0, "Max stop, NQ / NAS100 (index points)", group=gRisk, tooltip="v3: 20 -> 25. 20 is Luca DESCRIBING Mamba (4. 04:09); module 11 is Mamba DEMONSTRATING — 'a 25 point stop loss, which is solid... actually a really good number' (00:20-00:23), 'we have a 25 point stop' (01:43), and 20 pts at (06:50). A 20-pt cap rejects his own worked example. Same demonstrated-over-described precedent as v2's trail-mode fix. The source brackets 20-25 and refuses 64 (01:26); it does not pin it.")
maxStopYM = input.float(30.0, "Max stop, YM / US30 (index points)", group=gRisk, tooltip="'let's say 30 points on YM' (4. 04:09). SINGLE-SOURCED and Luca-relayed — module 11 has no YM worked example, so unlike NQ there is no demonstrated number to prefer. Unchanged in v3.")
beAtR     = input.float(1.0,  "Move to break-even at R",               group=gRisk, tooltip="'at worst, at the least, please put your stops to break even at a one to one point five at the worst' (11. 08:02). 1.0 is the stated trigger; 1.5 is the stated latest.")
lockAtR   = input.float(2.0,  "Start locking profit at R",             group=gRisk)
trailMode = input.string("Freeze at +1R (what he demonstrates)", "Trail rule above break-even", options=["Break-even only (11. 09:01)","Freeze at +1R (what he demonstrates)","Step every +1R (11. 02:13)"], group=gRisk,
     tooltip="The source supports all three; only the break-even floor is non-negotiable. See the TRAIL note in this file's header.")
maxTrades = input.int(2,      "Max trades per day (counts across NQ+YM)", group=gRisk)

gTgt = "Target — 10._USING_DATA"
useAdaptR = input.bool(true, "Target = rolling mean achieved R (his actual rule)", group=gTgt)
rrWindow  = input.int(6, "Trades in the window", group=gTgt, minval=1, maxval=8, tooltip="'the last two weeks of trades, which is typically anywhere from six to eight trades' (10. 00:38). His worked example uses 6.")
rTarget   = input.float(3.0, "Fallback / fixed target, R", group=gTgt, tooltip="Used until the window has filled, or if the adaptive rule is switched off.")

gV = "Display"
showDash = input.bool(true, "Dashboard",        group=gV)
showLvls = input.bool(true, "S/R levels",       group=gV)
showStruct=input.bool(true, "Structure labels", group=gV)
showTrade= input.bool(true, "Trade levels",     group=gV)
showLadder=input.bool(true, "Target ladder 1R-5R (his 'target one..five')", group=gV)
showBrkt = input.bool(true, "Counter-structure bracket (what the streams show)", group=gV)

// ── 0. INSTRUMENT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// v4 moved this block up from the risk section: the touch tolerance now resolves against the live
// max-stop cap, so the instrument must be known before the level block runs. Reads inputs and
// `syminfo` only — no behaviour change from v3.
// v2: resolved per instrument. 30 pts is ~0.14% of NQ and ~0.07% of YM — one number cannot serve
// both, and v1 applied 30 to whatever chart it was on.
tkr   = str.upper(syminfo.ticker)
autoYM= str.contains(tkr, "YM") or str.contains(tkr, "US30") or str.contains(tkr, "DJI") or str.contains(tkr, "DOW")
isYM  = instMode == "YM / US30" or (instMode == "Auto from ticker" and autoYM)
instNm= isYM ? "YM / US30" : "NQ / NAS100"
maxStopPts = isYM ? maxStopYM : maxStopNQ

// ── 1. SESSION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
inSess  = not useSession or not na(time(timeframe.period, sessTime, sessTZ))
newDay  = ta.change(time("1D")) != 0

// ── 2. MARKET STRUCTURE — higher highs / higher lows vs lower lows / lower highs ──────────────
ph = ta.pivothigh(high, pivLen, pivLen)
pl = ta.pivotlow(low,   pivLen, pivLen)

var float lastPH = na, var float prevPH = na
var float lastPL = na, var float prevPL = na
var int   lastPHbar = na, var int lastPLbar = na       // v2: needed to exclude a level's own pivot window

if not na(ph)
    prevPH := lastPH
    lastPH := ph
    lastPHbar := bar_index - pivLen
if not na(pl)
    prevPL := lastPL
    lastPL := pl
    lastPLbar := bar_index - pivLen

hh = not na(lastPH) and not na(prevPH) and lastPH > prevPH
lh = not na(lastPH) and not na(prevPH) and lastPH < prevPH
hl = not na(lastPL) and not na(prevPL) and lastPL > prevPL
ll = not na(lastPL) and not na(prevPL) and lastPL < prevPL

bullStruct = hh and hl          // "higher highs followed by higher lows"
bearStruct = ll and lh          // "lower low, lower high"
consolidating = not bullStruct and not bearStruct   // "the gray zone... we don't trade it"

if showStruct and not na(ph)
    label.new(bar_index - pivLen, ph, hh ? "HH" : lh ? "LH" : "H", style=label.style_label_down,
         color=color.new(hh ? color.green : color.red, 40), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
if showStruct and not na(pl)
    label.new(bar_index - pivLen, pl, hl ? "HL" : ll ? "LL" : "L", style=label.style_label_up,
         color=color.new(hl ? color.green : color.red, 40), textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)

// ── 3. LEVELS — validated by DISTINCT touches, excluding the level's own pivot window ─────────
// v1 counted every BAR inside the tolerance band, over a window that included the pivot's own
// formation neighbourhood — so a level was "validated" the moment it formed, with no revisits.
// He counts visits: "one touch two touch three four five six seven touches with those wicks"
// (7. 00:47) and "one touch two touch three touch four touch almost another touch" (7. 01:04).
// A visit = an entry into the band from outside it. Both counts are returned so the correction's
// magnitude is visible rather than asserted.
// v4: the band is now in the cap's units. In % mode it was 24.95 pts on NQ and 46.94 on YM at his
// own screen prices — wider than the stop budget those same levels have to carry, so the counter
// and the stop-width gate were describing the same level with numbers 2-3× apart. See FINDING 19.
// % mode is left byte-for-byte as v1-v3, close-anchoring defect included, so the diff is clean.
tol = tolMode == "% of price (v1-v3 behaviour)" ? close * touchTol / 100 : tolFrac * maxStopPts

f_touches(lvl, lvlBar) =>
    int nRaw  = 0
    int nDist = 0
    bool inBand = false
    if not na(lvl)
        for i = 199 to 0
            bi = bar_index - i
            skip = bi < 0 or (not na(lvlBar) and math.abs(bi - lvlBar) <= pivLen)
            if not skip
                near = math.abs(high[i] - lvl) <= tol or math.abs(low[i] - lvl) <= tol
                if near
                    nRaw += 1
                    if not inBand
                        nDist += 1
                        inBand := true
                else
                    inBand := false
    [nRaw, nDist]

resLvl = lastPH
supLvl = lastPL
[resRaw, resDist] = f_touches(resLvl, lastPHbar)
[supRaw, supDist] = f_touches(supLvl, lastPLbar)

useDist  = touchMode == "Distinct visits (v2, his definition)"
resCount = useDist ? resDist : resRaw
supCount = useDist ? supDist : supRaw
resValid = not na(resLvl) and resCount >= minTouch
supValid = not na(supLvl) and supCount >= minTouch

plot(showLvls and resValid ? resLvl : na, "Resistance", color=color.new(color.red,  0), style=plot.style_stepline, linewidth=2)
plot(showLvls and supValid ? supLvl : na, "Support",    color=color.new(color.green,0), style=plot.style_stepline, linewidth=2)

// ── 3b. THE ROLE FLIP — v1 advertised it in the header and never implemented it ───────────────
// "But guess what support resistance does it turns into each other?" (7. 01:51)
// "So support broke and then became resistance... they do very often" (7. 02:16-02:19)
// "Resistance now support... a break and a retest of support into resistance" (7. 07:14)
// A flipped level stays live until price closes back through it (the reclaim invalidates it).
var float flipRes = na, var float flipSup = na
// v4: `breakClears` (OFF by default) requires the close to clear the tolerance band, not merely
// the pivot price. With it off — the default, unchanged from v1-v3 — a close one tick past the
// pivot is a break on a bar the counter simultaneously scores as a touch of that same level.
resBrkPx = na(resLvl) ? na : resLvl + (breakClears ? tol : 0.0)
supBrkPx = na(supLvl) ? na : supLvl - (breakClears ? tol : 0.0)
brokeResRaw = resValid and ta.crossover(close,  resBrkPx)
brokeSupRaw = supValid and ta.crossunder(close, supBrkPx)
if brokeSupRaw
    flipRes := supLvl        // a broken floor becomes a ceiling
if brokeResRaw
    flipSup := resLvl        // a broken ceiling becomes a floor
if not na(flipRes) and close > flipRes
    flipRes := na
if not na(flipSup) and close < flipSup
    flipSup := na

plot(showFlip and not na(flipRes) ? flipRes : na, "Flipped resistance (was support)", color=color.new(color.orange, 20), style=plot.style_stepline, linewidth=1)
plot(showFlip and not na(flipSup) ? flipSup : na, "Flipped support (was resistance)", color=color.new(color.aqua,   20), style=plot.style_stepline, linewidth=1)

// ── 4. BREAK ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Optional: a flipped level may also carry a break. OFF by default — see the input tooltip.
brokeFlipL = flipTrades and not na(flipSup) and ta.crossover(close,  flipSup + (breakClears ? tol : 0.0))
brokeFlipS = flipTrades and not na(flipRes) and ta.crossunder(close, flipRes - (breakClears ? tol : 0.0))
brokeRes = brokeResRaw or brokeFlipL
brokeSup = brokeSupRaw or brokeFlipS
// the level a long/short would actually be stopped behind
brkLvlLong  = brokeFlipL and not brokeResRaw ? flipSup : resLvl
brkLvlShort = brokeFlipS and not brokeSupRaw ? flipRes : supLvl

// ── 5. VOLUME ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
volAvg = ta.sma(volume, volLen)
volOK  = not useVol or (not na(volAvg) and volAvg > 0 and volume > volAvg * volMult)
volRat = (na(volAvg) or volAvg == 0) ? na : volume / volAvg

// ── DAILY TRADE COUNTER — "up to two trades max per day" ─────────────────────────────────────
var int tradesToday = 0
if newDay
    tradesToday := 0
underCap = tradesToday < maxTrades

// ── ROLLING ACHIEVED-R WINDOW — 10._USING_DATA, the rule that actually sets the target ───────
// "I only calculated the second number. I don't care about the one." (10. 02:48)
// "We take the three, ZERO FOR A LOSS, two point five, five, five and a three." (10. 02:56)
// "That equals 18.5. We divide that by six... we are averaging a one, two, three." (10. 03:47)
// Eight shift registers rather than an array: arrays are on this project's forbidden list.
// NOTE: he says "median" (10. 00:52, 05:59) and computes the arithmetic MEAN every time. His own
// example cannot tell them apart ({0,2.5,3,3,5,5}: mean 3.083, median 3.0, both called "one to
// three"). Mechanising the arithmetic he performs, not the word he uses. See SYSTEM.md FINDING 7.
var float r1 = na, var float r2 = na, var float r3 = na, var float r4 = na
var float r5 = na, var float r6 = na, var float r7 = na, var float r8 = na

sumR = (rrWindow >= 1 and not na(r1) ? r1 : 0.0) + (rrWindow >= 2 and not na(r2) ? r2 : 0.0) +
       (rrWindow >= 3 and not na(r3) ? r3 : 0.0) + (rrWindow >= 4 and not na(r4) ? r4 : 0.0) +
       (rrWindow >= 5 and not na(r5) ? r5 : 0.0) + (rrWindow >= 6 and not na(r6) ? r6 : 0.0) +
       (rrWindow >= 7 and not na(r7) ? r7 : 0.0) + (rrWindow >= 8 and not na(r8) ? r8 : 0.0)
cntR = (rrWindow >= 1 and not na(r1) ? 1 : 0) + (rrWindow >= 2 and not na(r2) ? 1 : 0) +
       (rrWindow >= 3 and not na(r3) ? 1 : 0) + (rrWindow >= 4 and not na(r4) ? 1 : 0) +
       (rrWindow >= 5 and not na(r5) ? 1 : 0) + (rrWindow >= 6 and not na(r6) ? 1 : 0) +
       (rrWindow >= 7 and not na(r7) ? 1 : 0) + (rrWindow >= 8 and not na(r8) ? 1 : 0)

avgAchR   = cntR > 0 ? sumR / cntR : na
windowFull= cntR >= rrWindow
// "we are averaging a one, two, three... we are going to go for one, two, threes" — rounded to a
// whole R, floored at 1 so a bad window cannot produce a sub-1R target he never trades.
rTargetUse = useAdaptR and windowFull and not na(avgAchR) ? math.max(1.0, math.round(avgAchR)) : rTarget

// ── THE STOP-WIDTH GATE — a setup whose structure sits too far away is REJECTED, not re-stopped ─
// "That's a 25 point stop loss, which is solid." (11. 00:07)
// "64 points. No, my account's gone if I do that." (11. 01:26)
// The instrument and its cap are resolved in section 0 — v4 moved that block above the level
// block because the touch tolerance now depends on the cap.
//
// v3: ONE definition of the pad, in the cap's own units by default. v2 wrote this expression
// twice — here and inline in the trade-open block — so the two could silently diverge.
// In % mode the pad is 12.48 pts at NQ 24,954.50 and 23.47 pts at YM 46,942 (both read off his
// own screen, 4. 03:06 / 07:23), i.e. 62% and 78% of the entire max-stop budget before any
// structural distance is counted, rising with price until pad >= cap makes the gate impossible.
padNow      = padMode == "% of price (v1/v2 behaviour)" ? close * stopPad / 100 : padTicks * syminfo.mintick
padPct      = maxStopPts <= 0 ? na : 100 * padNow / maxStopPts   // share of the cap the pad eats
stopBudget  = maxStopPts - padNow                                // pts left for (entry - level)
projStopL   = na(brkLvlLong)  ? na : brkLvlLong  - padNow   // long stops below the broken level
projStopS   = na(brkLvlShort) ? na : brkLvlShort + padNow   // short stops above the broken level
projRlong   = na(projStopL) ? na : math.abs(close - projStopL)
projRshort  = na(projStopS) ? na : math.abs(close - projStopS)
stopOKlong  = not useMaxStop or (not na(projRlong)  and projRlong  <= maxStopPts)
stopOKshort = not useMaxStop or (not na(projRshort) and projRshort <= maxStopPts)

// v4 instrumentation — the commensurability test between the two gates. `tol` is the level's own
// positional uncertainty; `stopBudget` is the most a break may sit beyond that level and still be
// accepted. If tol > stopBudget then every tradeable break lies inside the band the counter still
// calls a touch, which is what v1-v3 shipped on both instruments (−0.20 pts NQ, −17.94 pts YM).
tolPct    = maxStopPts <= 0 ? na : 100 * tol / maxStopPts     // half-band as a share of the cap
bandPts   = 2 * tol                                           // full band width
tolFitsBudget = tol <= stopBudget

// ── THE SIGNAL ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
goLong  = inSess and bullStruct and brokeRes and volOK and underCap and stopOKlong
goShort = inSess and bearStruct and brokeSup and volOK and underCap and stopOKshort

// The break he would have marked on the OTHER side, which the course's structure gate forbids.
// Drawn, never traded — see the header note on the stated-vs-observed contradiction.
brktLvl = bullStruct ? supLvl : bearStruct ? resLvl : na
plot(showBrkt and not na(brktLvl) ? brktLvl : na, "Counter-structure bracket",
     color=color.new(color.gray, 35), style=plot.style_circles, linewidth=1)

// ── SIMULATED TRADE — so stop, target and the trail rule can be drawn ────────────────────────
var int   dir     = 0
var float entryPx = na, var float stopPx = na, var float tgtPx = na, var float initR = na
var float tgtR    = na                       // the target THIS trade was opened against
var line  lnE = na, var line  lnS = na, var line  lnT = na
var line  lad1 = na, var line lad2 = na, var line lad3 = na, var line lad4 = na, var line lad5 = na

curR = dir == 0 or na(initR) or initR == 0 ? na : (dir == 1 ? (close - entryPx) : (entryPx - close)) / initR
// v2 fix: manage on the PREVIOUS bar's R. v1 moved the stop using this bar's close and then
// tested this bar's low against it, booking exits on lows that preceded the move that caused them.
curRprev = dir == 0 or na(initR) or initR == 0 ? na : (dir == 1 ? (close[1] - entryPx) : (entryPx - close[1])) / initR

// manage the stop — see the TRAIL note in the header; the mode is an input because the source
// genuinely supports three readings and only the break-even floor is stated as non-negotiable.
if dir != 0 and not na(curRprev)
    float wantR = na
    if curRprev >= beAtR
        wantR := 0.0                                              // break-even (11. 02:28 / 08:02)
    if trailMode != "Break-even only (11. 09:01)" and curRprev >= lockAtR
        wantR := 1.0                                              // lock +1R (11. 03:21 / 06:38)
    if trailMode == "Step every +1R (11. 02:13)" and curRprev >= lockAtR
        wantR := math.max(1.0, math.floor(curRprev) - 1.0)         // step with it (11. 02:13 / 03:59)
    if not na(wantR)
        newStop = dir == 1 ? entryPx + wantR * initR : entryPx - wantR * initR
        stopPx := dir == 1 ? math.max(stopPx, newStop) : math.min(stopPx, newStop)

hitT = dir ==  1 and high >= tgtPx  or dir == -1 and low  <= tgtPx
hitS = dir ==  1 and low  <= stopPx or dir == -1 and high >= stopPx

if dir != 0 and (hitT or hitS)
    // v2 fix: an ambiguous bar (both touched) books the STOP, not the target. Achieved R feeds the
    // rolling-mean target, so an optimistic tie-break biases the target upward on every such bar.
    outR = hitS ? (dir == 1 ? (stopPx - entryPx) : (entryPx - stopPx)) / initR : tgtR
    txt  = not hitS ? "TARGET +" + str.tostring(tgtR, "#.#") + "R"
             : outR > 0.001  ? "TRAIL +" + str.tostring(outR, "#.#") + "R"
             : outR > -0.001 ? "BREAK-EVEN" : "STOP −1R"
    label.new(bar_index, dir == 1 ? high : low, txt, style = dir == 1 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up,
         color = outR > 0 ? color.new(color.teal, 20) : color.new(color.maroon, 20), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
    if not na(lnE)
        line.set_x2(lnE, bar_index), line.set_x2(lnS, bar_index), line.set_x2(lnT, bar_index)
    if not na(lad1)
        line.set_x2(lad1, bar_index), line.set_x2(lad2, bar_index), line.set_x2(lad3, bar_index)
        line.set_x2(lad4, bar_index), line.set_x2(lad5, bar_index)
    // push the achieved R into his rolling window — a loss scores 0, per 10. 02:56
    r8 := r7
    r7 := r6
    r6 := r5
    r5 := r4
    r4 := r3
    r3 := r2
    r2 := r1
    r1 := math.max(outR, 0)
    dir := 0

if dir == 0 and (goLong or goShort)
    dir     := goLong ? 1 : -1
    entryPx := close
    lvl      = goLong ? brkLvlLong : brkLvlShort
    pad      = padNow                             // v3: one definition, not a second copy of the formula
    stopPx  := goLong ? lvl - pad : lvl + pad     // "our stop loss is below where it would come
                                                  //  back to retest" (7. 05:43) — the broken level,
                                                  //  never the far one
    initR   := math.abs(entryPx - stopPx)
    tgtR    := rTargetUse
    tgtPx   := goLong ? entryPx + initR * tgtR : entryPx - initR * tgtR
    tradesToday += 1
    if showTrade
        lnE := line.new(bar_index, entryPx, bar_index+1, entryPx, color=color.blue,  width=2)
        lnS := line.new(bar_index, stopPx,  bar_index+1, stopPx,  color=color.red,   width=2, style=line.style_dashed)
        lnT := line.new(bar_index, tgtPx,   bar_index+1, tgtPx,   color=color.green, width=2, style=line.style_dashed)
    if showLadder
        // "target one... target two... target three... target four... target five" — all five NY
        // streams. He scales out along these rungs; 10._USING_DATA decides which one calls the day.
        // NOTE: this simulator exits in ONE piece at tgtR. The ladder is drawn, not traded — a
        // scale-out would make "achieved R" a blend, and nothing in the source says the weights.
        s = dir
        lad1 := line.new(bar_index, entryPx + s*initR*1, bar_index+1, entryPx + s*initR*1, color=color.new(color.olive,50), style=line.style_dotted)
        lad2 := line.new(bar_index, entryPx + s*initR*2, bar_index+1, entryPx + s*initR*2, color=color.new(color.olive,50), style=line.style_dotted)
        lad3 := line.new(bar_index, entryPx + s*initR*3, bar_index+1, entryPx + s*initR*3, color=color.new(color.olive,50), style=line.style_dotted)
        lad4 := line.new(bar_index, entryPx + s*initR*4, bar_index+1, entryPx + s*initR*4, color=color.new(color.olive,50), style=line.style_dotted)
        lad5 := line.new(bar_index, entryPx + s*initR*5, bar_index+1, entryPx + s*initR*5, color=color.new(color.olive,50), style=line.style_dotted)
    label.new(bar_index, goLong ? low : high,
         (goLong ? "▲ LONG break " : "▼ SHORT break ") + str.tostring(lvl, format.mintick) + "  #" + str.tostring(tradesToday),
         style = goLong ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down,
         color = goLong ? color.new(color.green,10) : color.new(color.red,10), textcolor=color.white)

if dir != 0 and not na(lnE)
    line.set_x2(lnE, bar_index), line.set_x2(lnS, bar_index), line.set_x2(lnT, bar_index)
    line.set_y1(lnS, stopPx), line.set_y2(lnS, stopPx)
if dir != 0 and not na(lad1)
    line.set_x2(lad1, bar_index), line.set_x2(lad2, bar_index), line.set_x2(lad3, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lad4, bar_index), line.set_x2(lad5, bar_index)

// ── SHADING ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bgcolor(useSession and not inSess ? color.new(color.gray, 90) : na,  title="Outside New York session")
bgcolor(inSess and consolidating  ? color.new(color.orange, 90) : na,title="Consolidation — no trade")
bgcolor(inSess and bullStruct     ? color.new(color.green, 94) : na, title="Bullish structure")
bgcolor(inSess and bearStruct     ? color.new(color.red, 94) : na,   title="Bearish structure")
barcolor(useVol and not volOK ? color.new(color.gray, 50) : na,      title="No volume")

// ── DASHBOARD ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var table d = table.new(position.top_right, 3, 17, border_width=1, frame_width=1, frame_color=color.gray)
f_row(t, r, k, ok, v) =>
    table.cell(t, 0, r, k, text_color=color.white,  text_size=size.small, bgcolor=color.new(color.black,20), text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(t, 1, r, ok ? "✔" : "✖", text_color=ok ? color.lime : color.red, text_size=size.small, bgcolor=color.new(color.black,20))
    table.cell(t, 2, r, v, text_color=color.silver, text_size=size.small, bgcolor=color.new(color.black,20), text_halign=text.align_left)

f_tch(lvl, dst, raw) =>
    na(lvl) ? "—" : str.tostring(lvl, format.mintick) + "   " + str.tostring(dst) + " visits / " + str.tostring(raw) + " bars-in-band  (need " + str.tostring(minTouch) + ")"

if showDash and barstate.islast
    st = bullStruct ? "BULLISH — buys only" : bearStruct ? "BEARISH — sells only" : "CONSOLIDATION"
    tfOK = timeframe.period == "5" or timeframe.period == "15"
    table.cell(d, 0, 0, "LEGACY FOREX", text_color=color.white, text_size=size.normal, bgcolor=color.new(color.blue,30), text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(d, 1, 0, syminfo.ticker,  text_color=color.white, text_size=size.normal, bgcolor=color.new(color.blue,30))
    table.cell(d, 2, 0, dir==1?"IN LONG":dir==-1?"IN SHORT":"flat", text_color=color.white, text_size=size.normal, bgcolor=color.new(color.blue,30), text_halign=text.align_left)

    f_row(d, 1, "Session",    inSess,       inSess ? "New York — live" : "outside NY — no trades")
    f_row(d, 2, "Timeframe",  tfOK,         timeframe.period + "m" + (tfOK ? "" : "  ← he trades 5m/15m ONLY"))
    f_row(d, 3, "Instrument", true,         syminfo.ticker + "  → read as " + instNm + ", max stop " + str.tostring(maxStopPts, "#") + " pts")
    f_row(d, 4, "Structure",  not consolidating, st)
    f_row(d, 5, "Resistance", resValid,     f_tch(resLvl, resDist, resRaw))
    f_row(d, 6, "Support",    supValid,     f_tch(supLvl, supDist, supRaw))
    f_row(d, 7, "Flipped",    not na(flipRes) or not na(flipSup),
         (na(flipRes) ? "" : "res " + str.tostring(flipRes, format.mintick) + "  ") +
         (na(flipSup) ? "" : "sup " + str.tostring(flipSup, format.mintick) + "  ") +
         (na(flipRes) and na(flipSup) ? "none live" : (flipTrades ? "(can fire)" : "(drawn only)")))
    f_row(d, 8, "Break",      brokeRes or brokeSup, brokeRes ? "broke RESISTANCE ✓" : brokeSup ? "broke SUPPORT ✓" : "waiting for a break")
    f_row(d, 9, "Volume",     volOK,        na(volRat) ? "—" : str.tostring(volRat, "#.##") + "× avg  (need > " + str.tostring(volMult, "#.##") + ")")
    // which side's stop width is the live question depends on which side structure permits
    projR    = bullStruct ? projRlong : bearStruct ? projRshort : na
    stopOKnow= bullStruct ? stopOKlong : bearStruct ? stopOKshort : true
    f_row(d, 10, "Stop width", stopOKnow, na(projR) ? "—" : str.tostring(projR, "#.#") + " pts  (max " + str.tostring(maxStopPts, "#") + " — he refused 64)")
    // v3 instrumentation: the pad and the cap were in different units, and the pad was eating most
    // of the budget. This row makes that visible so a zero-signal chart can be attributed to the
    // right gate instead of being confused with v2's touch-counting correction.
    f_row(d, 11, "Stop budget", stopBudget > 0,
         str.tostring(padNow, "#.##") + " pts pad (" + str.tostring(padPct, "#") + "% of cap)  →  "
         + (stopBudget > 0 ? str.tostring(stopBudget, "#.#") + " pts left for entry-to-level"
                           : "PAD ≥ CAP — no setup can ever pass"))
    // v4 instrumentation: the touch tolerance was a % of price while everything it has to be
    // commensurable with is in index points. This row is the third and last zero-signal cause on
    // the dashboard, so a blank chart can now be attributed rather than guessed at.
    f_row(d, 12, "Level width", tolFitsBudget,
         "±" + str.tostring(tol, "#.##") + " pts  (band " + str.tostring(bandPts, "#.#") + ", "
         + str.tostring(tolPct, "#") + "% of cap)  →  "
         + (tolFitsBudget ? "fits inside the " + str.tostring(stopBudget, "#.#") + "-pt stop budget"
                          : "TOL > BUDGET — every tradeable break is still inside the touch band"))
    f_row(d, 13, "Target",    true,      (useAdaptR ? (windowFull ? "1:" + str.tostring(rTargetUse, "#") + "  from mean " + str.tostring(avgAchR, "#.##") + "R of last " + str.tostring(cntR) + " (10._USING_DATA)"
                                                                  : "1:" + str.tostring(rTargetUse, "#") + "  FALLBACK — window " + str.tostring(cntR) + "/" + str.tostring(rrWindow) + " trades")
                                                    : "1:" + str.tostring(rTargetUse, "#") + "  fixed (adaptive rule off)"))
    f_row(d, 14, "Trail rule", true,      trailMode + "   (source is ambiguous — see header)")
    f_row(d, 15, "Trades today", underCap, str.tostring(tradesToday) + " / " + str.tostring(maxTrades) + "  (cap counts across NQ+YM)")

    // name the FIRST unmet condition, in his own order, so the dashboard says what is blocking
    blocker = not inSess        ? "NO TRADE — outside New York session"
      : consolidating           ? "NO TRADE — consolidation"
      : not (resValid or supValid) ? "WAIT — no level has " + str.tostring(minTouch) + " distinct touches yet"
      : not (brokeRes or brokeSup) ? "WAIT — no break of a validated level"
      : not volOK               ? "NO TRADE — no volume"
      : not stopOKnow           ? "NO TRADE — stop too wide (" + str.tostring(projR, "#.#") + " pts)"
      : not underCap            ? "NO TRADE — daily cap reached"
      : "WAIT"
    verdict = goLong ? "▲ LONG NOW" : goShort ? "▼ SHORT NOW" : dir != 0 ? ("HOLDING  " + (na(curR)?"":str.tostring(curR,"#.##") + "R  → 1:" + str.tostring(tgtR,"#"))) : blocker
    vc = goLong ? color.green : goShort ? color.red : dir != 0 ? color.blue : color.new(color.gray,40)
    table.cell(d, 0, 16, "VERDICT", text_color=color.white, text_size=size.normal, bgcolor=vc, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(d, 1, 16, "", bgcolor=vc)
    table.cell(d, 2, 16, verdict, text_color=color.white, text_size=size.normal, bgcolor=vc, text_halign=text.align_left)

alertcondition(goLong,  "Legacy LONG",  "Legacy Forex: LONG — structure bullish, resistance broken, volume present")
alertcondition(goShort, "Legacy SHORT", "Legacy Forex: SHORT — structure bearish, support broken, volume present")

plot(goLong ? 1:0,  "LongSignal",  display=display.data_window)
plot(goShort ? 1:0, "ShortSignal", display=display.data_window)
plot(curR,          "CurrentR",    display=display.data_window)
plot(avgAchR,       "MeanAchievedR (10._USING_DATA)", display=display.data_window)
plot(rTargetUse,    "TargetR in use", display=display.data_window)
plot(bullStruct ? projRlong : bearStruct ? projRshort : na, "ProjectedStopPts", display=display.data_window)
// v2 instrumentation — the numbers a forward test needs to settle the touch-counting correction
plot(resDist,       "ResTouches distinct", display=display.data_window)
plot(resRaw,        "ResTouches bars-in-band (v1)", display=display.data_window)
plot(supDist,       "SupTouches distinct", display=display.data_window)
plot(supRaw,        "SupTouches bars-in-band (v1)", display=display.data_window)
// v3 instrumentation — separates the stop-width gate from the touch gate as a zero-signal cause
plot(padNow,        "Pad (pts)",              display=display.data_window)
plot(padPct,        "Pad as % of max stop",   display=display.data_window)
plot(stopBudget,    "Stop budget left (pts)", display=display.data_window)
// v4 instrumentation — the level's own width, in the same units as everything it must fit inside
plot(tol,           "Touch tolerance (pts, half-band)", display=display.data_window)
plot(bandPts,       "Touch band width (pts)",           display=display.data_window)
plot(tolPct,        "Tolerance as % of max stop",       display=display.data_window)
plot(tolFitsBudget ? 1 : 0, "TolFitsStopBudget",        display=display.data_window)
